+---
+title: "Aegis Vendor DPA — Non‑Training & BYOK Clauses (Draft)"
+---
+
+Purpose: Provide Legal / Procurement draft clauses to require vendors to avoid training on customer data, enable BYOK, and support audit & deletion.
+
+1. Non-Training Clause
+- Vendor shall not use Customer Data to train, improve, fine-tune, or otherwise modify any machine learning models (including Vendor's internal models) without the Customer's prior written consent. This prohibition includes using Customer Data for supervised, unsupervised, self-supervised, reinforcement learning, or any other learning technique.
+
+2. BYOK / Key Handling
+- Vendor shall support Customer-Provided Keys (BYOK) for encryption at rest and in transit where applicable. Vendor must accept the Customer's key material or key reference and must not export Customer key material outside the Customer's control. Any vendor access to decrypted data must be logged and require dual‑control approval for sensitive operations.
+
+3. Logging & Deletion
+- Vendor must provide APIs and contractual guarantees to delete Customer Data upon request within [X] days and to provide proof of deletion. Vendor shall also enable Customer to export logs (request/response, metadata) for audit within [Y] days.
+
+4. Subprocessors & Residency
+- Vendor shall provide a current list of subprocessors and seek Customer approval for new subprocessors. Data processing shall occur only in regions agreed by Customer.
+
+5. Audit Rights & Certifications
+- Vendor must maintain SOC 2 Type II and ISO 27001 and provide audit reports on request. Customer or a mutually agreed third‑party auditor may perform an audit annually, subject to reasonable confidentiality constraints.
+
+6. Incident Notification
+- Vendor shall notify Customer of security incidents affecting Customer Data within 72 hours and cooperate in remediation and forensic analysis.
+
+7. Remedies
+- Material breach of non-training or BYOK obligations permits Customer to suspend services and terminate the Agreement for cause and require deletion of any derivatively trained artifacts.
+
+Provide this draft to Legal & Procurement for negotiation with Anthropic / OpenAI / Google or other LLM vendors.
